e and ensure there are no hidden bugs or edge cases thus far in development and optimize the code where it would be beneficial to performance and stability\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n# Continuation Summary\n\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Comprehensive Code Audit, Bug Detection, and Performance/Stability Optimization:**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"I need you to step through this code line by line, function by function, module by module and ensure there are no hidden bugs or edge cases thus far in development and optimize the code where it would be beneficial to performance and stability\"`\n  - *Status:* **DISCOVERY & IMPLEMENTATION** (Audited `leadsRepository.ts`, `database.ts`, `backupService.ts`, `visionService.ts`, `SettingsScreen.tsx`, and `ListsScreen.tsx`; in progress reviewing `DialerHudScreen.tsx`, `aiSmsService.ts`, and `ScanSheetScreen.tsx` for state leaks, unhandled async errors, and navigation parameter edge cases).\n- **Auto-Deploy Rule (Standing Directive):**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"deploy it to surge please...and do so going forward after every new compile\"`\n  - *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION** (Every new build must be exported with `npx expo export -p web`, injected with PWA meta tags in `dist/index.html` and `dist/manifest.json`, and deployed via `npx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n- **Domain & Rules:**\n  - Target Company: **ValuTeachers** working with Florida educators on the **Florida Retirement System (FRS)** and **403(b)/457(b)** plans.\n  - Call Goal: **45-minute planning period in-person classroom sit-down**.\n  - **Single Lead Workflow:** Snapping photos captures 1 report card at a time. The app treats all records as flat individual educator leads in a master pipeline, not discrete \"lists\".\n  - **Zero Test Data Mandate:** The user explicitly commanded: `\"why does maria gonzalez, david sterling and joseph adona keep appearing after delete. test/fake data should no longer be used AT ALL in this development\"`. No hardcoded dummy data should ever be auto-seeded or returned as fallback.\n  - **Live Surge Domain:** `https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`.\n  - **Multi-Source Backup & Recovery:** The user required full export and import support across iCloud Drive, Google Drive, OneDrive, email attachments, clipboard text, with Merge vs Overwrite options.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n1. **Resolved Bootloader Blank Screen & Added Root ErrorBoundary:**\n   - Removed blocking startup gate `if (!dbReady)` in `App.tsx`.\n   - Wrapped `App.tsx` in a React `ErrorBoundary` component displaying clear error details when unhandled runtime errors occur.\n2. **Fixed Missing Module Imports:**\n   - Fixed `Can't find variable: ScrollView` in `ListsScreen.tsx` by adding `ScrollView` to `react-native` imports.\n   - Fixed `Can't find variable: Trash2` in `SettingsScreen.tsx` by adding `Trash2` to `lucide-react-native` imports.\n3. **Completely Eradicated All Mock/Demo Contacts:**\n   - Removed `sampleLeads` (Joseph Adona, Maria Gonzalez, David Sterling) from `database.ts` initialization.\n   - Removed `getDemoExtractedLeads()` and mock fallback logic from `visionService.ts`.\n   - Added a red **\"Wipe All Leads & Start Fresh\"** button in `SettingsScreen.tsx` to wipe any previously cached test contacts.\n4. **Built Full Database Backup Export & Multi-Source Recovery System:**\n   - Updated `backupService.ts` and `SettingsScreen.tsx` with:\n     - Full JSON file download & Native Share Sheet integration (Files, iCloud Drive, Google Drive, OneDrive, Mail).\n     - 1-tap clipboard JSON copy and modal for pasting raw backup text.\n     - Web file picker (`<input type=\"file\" accept=\".json\">`) to restore directly from iCloud/Google Drive/OneDrive files.\n     - Support for **Merge with Existing** vs **Clean Overwrite** restoration modes.\n5. **Surge Deployments:**\n   - Successfully built and deployed all patches live to `https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n- **WebDatabase Storage Layer (`src/db/database.ts`):**\n  - Uses `localStorage.getItem('snap_dialer_valuteachers_data')` for web persistence.\n  - `getAllAsync` supports SQL pattern matching for `FROM leads`, `FROM lists`, `FROM call_logs`, `FROM sms_templates`, and `FROM settings`.\n  - `runAsync` handles SQL inserts, updates, and deletes for leads, logs, templates, and settings.\n  - Arrays are defensively validated with `Array.isArray()` so corrupt JSON or legacy structures do not crash the app.\n- **Leads Repository (`src/db/leadsRepository.ts`):**\n  - `addSingleLead` inserts individual leads with `list_id = 'master_queue'`.\n  - `getMasterDialingQueue` selects leads where `last_disposition` is `pending`, `no_answer`, or `voicemail`.\n  - `hydrateLead` parses JSON strings for `frs_interests` and `meeting_preferences` safely.\n- **Surge Deploy Pipeline:**\n  1. `npx expo export -p web` (in `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer`)\n  2. Inject standalone PWA tags (`apple-mobile-web-app-capable`) into `dist/index.html`\n  3. Ensure `dist/manifest.json` exists\n  4. `npx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- `src/db/database.ts`: Removed all mock lead seeding; enhanced `loadFromStorage` and `runAsync` field parsing.\n- `src/services/visionService.ts`: Removed `getDemoExtractedLeads()` and mock fallback.\n- `src/services/backupService.ts`: Added `generateBackupPayload`, file browser picker `importBackupFromFile`, clipboard copy, and merge/overwrite restore logic.\n- `src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx`: Added `Trash2` import, backup export buttons, clipboard copy, file import, JSON paste modal, and database wipe tools.\n- `src/screens/ListsScreen.tsx`: Added `ScrollView` import for filter tabs.\n- `App.tsx`: Added root `ErrorBoundary` and removed blocking boot check.\n- `dist/index.html` & `dist/manifest.json`: Injected iOS standalone PWA headers.\n\n### Viewed Files\n- `src/db/leadsRepository.ts` (Lines 1–324): Core data access layer for adding leads, queues, dispositions, and follow-ups.\n- `src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx` (Lines 1–1476): Power dialer HUD with swipe gesture controller, call timer, auto-advance, script tabs, and AI SMS generator.\n- `src/screens/ScanSheetScreen.tsx` (Lines 1–563): Report card photo scanner, camera trigger, and manual lead verification review form.\n- `src/screens/AnalyticsScreen.tsx` (Lines 1–250): Analytics dashboard with dial counts, connection rates, and export summary.\n- `src/screens/CadenceSettingsScreen.tsx` (Lines 1–321): Automated SMS cadence rules and template management.\n- `src/screens/LeadDetailScreen.tsx` (Lines 1–1055): Educator lead profile editor and full call log timeline.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n1. **Continue Line-by-Line Code Audit for Hidden Bugs & Optimization:**\n   - Audit `src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`:\n     - Check timer cleanup on unmount (`countdownTimerRef`, `callTimerRef`).\n     - Check `panResponder` release handlers on web touch events.\n     - Check AI SMS generation fallback if Gemini API key is missing or invalid.\n   - Audit `src/screens/ScanSheetScreen.tsx`:\n     - Check camera/image picker permissions and base64 compression handling on mobile web.\n     - Check lead verification input handling (numbers vs strings for `years_in_frs` and `phone`).\n   - Audit `src/services/telephonyService.ts` and `src/services/aiSmsService.ts`:\n     - Check `Linking.openURL` url encoding for SMS and tel schemas on iOS Safari (`sms:?&body=` vs `sms:;body=`).\n2. **Compile, Re-Test, and Deploy to Surge:**\n   - Run `npx expo export -p web`.\n   - Update `dist/index.html` and `dist/manifest.json`.\n   - Run `npx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`.\n\nYou have the 4 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787239731075]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e